{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## DESCRIPTION SUBSTANTIALLY REWRITTEN (epic e369 plan-review passes 2-8) — re-read before implementing\n\nThree defects in the original plan were found and fixed. Do not work from a cached reading.\n\n**1. The move set was wrong.** It listed `outbound_fields.py` and `comment_limits.py` and claimed *'none of these modules is reached by lazy_load / _load_sibling_keyed / spec_from_file_location'*. **That was false.** Verified by grep:\n- `adapters/jira/adf.py` <- `inbound_fields.py:36`, `outbound_fields.py:69`, ~13 test files\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py` <- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_config.py:193`, `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_roundtrip.py:72`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_commits_on_ticket.py:121`\n- `adapters/jira/comment_limits.py` <- ~9 test files\n\nMoving any of them breaks the dynamic loader. They now stay put and are shared by **dependency inversion**.\n\n**2. `jira_fields.py` cannot relocate wholesale** — it imports `fit_text_to_adf_limit` from the pinned `adf.py` and `truncate_comment_body`/`_JIRA_COMMENT_MAX_CHARS` from the pinned `comment_limits.py`, so moving it would make `jira_family/` import `adapters/jira/` — inverting the dependency direction this story's own oracle forbids. **The move is now by SYMBOL:** `_sanitize_label`, `_sanitize_summary`, `InvalidLabelError`, `_RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK` and the map literals move outright; `_sanitize_description`/`_sanitize_comment` move **contract-parameterized** (the codec/limit dependency is injected). `adapters/jira/jira_fields.py` **survives** as the thin Cloud-side contract-construction site. `probe.py` splits too — the classifier moves taking the resolved-status set as a **parameter**; `probe()`/`_resolve_env()` stay (they read Cloud ACLI settings).\n\n**3. Self-contradiction:** it asserted `acli*.py` are *byte-identical* while relocating the very symbols `acli.py:69-70` and `acli_cli_ops.py:34` import, with no shims. Impossible. The invariant is now **'no behavioral change to the ACLI transport'**, verified as an **import-only diff** (`git diff -U0` shows no added/removed line outside an import statement).\n\n### Two things that will bite an implementer\n\n- **The new import into pinned modules MUST be absolute**, never relative. Those modules are loaded via `spec_from_file_location` under synthetic names with `__package__ == ''`. I verified empirically that absolute `from rebar_reconciler...` imports resolve there (the conftest puts the engine dir on `sys.path`); a relative import raises `ImportError: attempted relative import with no known parent package`.\n- **The `deleted` key is a decided behavior change, not a pure move.** The unified map adopts `deleted -> Done` (matching `outbound_fields` and `config.py:37`). The ACLI path's current `.title()` fallback yields `\"Deleted\"`, which is not a live DIG workflow state. Keep the fallback — it also passes already-Jira names like `\"In Progress\"` through unchanged — but pin the new `deleted` value with a test.\n\n### Blocked\n\nCannot be plan-reviewed until **J1 `acb2` closes** — `review-plan` fast-fails `INDETERMINATE` (`blocked by unclosed ticket(s) acb2`) with no LLM spend. J1's oracle is merged-pending at Gerrit change 1009; record its change number here before pushing this story (epic AC8)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785338278771556001,"uuid":"b9c4bcd5-c381-4966-b01d-e6def8e0a4e4"}